//! Codex App Server connector (official `codex app-server`, JSON-RPC over stdio).
//!
//! Rust drives the app-server directly — no ACP adapter, no sidecar. Wire facts below come from
//! the schema generated by the installed CLI (`codex app-server generate-json-schema`) and are
//! pinned by the fixtures in `tests/native_provider_connectors.rs`:
//!
//! - `initialize` → `initialized`, then `thread/start` | `thread/resume`, `turn/start`,
//!   `turn/steer` (requires `expectedTurnId`, answers `{turnId}`), `turn/interrupt` (empty ack).
//! - The terminal for a turn is the `turn/completed` notification (`completed | interrupted |
//!   failed`), never the response to `turn/start` or `turn/interrupt`.
//! - Approvals/questions are server→client *requests* that park the turn until answered.
//!
//! Honesty rules: a transport that closes after `turn/start` was queued is [`TurnOutcome::Unknown`]
//! and is never replayed here; an interrupt/steer request is not proof of a stop/adoption; a
//! dismissed or unreachable approval becomes `cancel` (a denial), never an accept.

